  "terms_section_1_body": "1.1. By accessing, installing or using the Mooze Wallet application (the \"App\"), the User represents that the User has read, understood and fully accepted these Terms of Use (the \"Terms\") and the accompanying Privacy Policy.\n\n1.2. Use of the App constitutes express, informed, conscious and irrevocable acceptance of all provisions contained in this document.\n\n1.3. If the User does not agree with any provision of these Terms, the User must immediately cease using the App, uninstall it from the User's devices and refrain from any interaction with the Services. Continued use of the App after the publication of these Terms or of subsequently updated versions constitutes full agreement with the terms then in effect.\n\n1.4. These Terms constitute a binding international contract between the User and Mooze Labs LLC, governed exclusively by the laws of the Republic of the Marshall Islands (\"RMI\"), within the limits set forth in Section 13.\n\n1.5. The User acknowledges that the User obtained the App through freely available and known information, by the User's own final decision, and is the sole capable responsible party.",
  "terms_section_2_body": "2.1. Mooze Labs LLC (\"Mooze\") is a limited liability company duly organized under the Associations Law of the Republic of the Marshall Islands (Title 52, Marshall Islands Revised Code), RMI.\n\n2.2. Mooze acts exclusively as a provider of software services (Software-as-a-Service). Its activity consists of the development, maintenance and provision of technology infrastructure for the operation of self-custodial digital wallets on the Bitcoin, Liquid Network and Lightning Network networks, as well as the programmatic orchestration of software calls (API calls) between the User's device and third-party infrastructures.\n\n2.3. Mooze IS NOT, does not operate as, does not hold itself out as, and shall not be construed as:\n(a) a brokerage, exchange, trading venue, trading platform, market maker or liquidity platform for digital assets;\n(b) a financial institution, payment institution, credit company, credit cooperative or equivalent entity;\n(c) a foreign exchange service provider, foreign exchange house or foreign exchange operator;\n(d) a money transmitter or money services business (MSB);\n(e) a Virtual Asset Service Provider (VASP) within the meaning of the Banking (Amendment) Act, 2020 — P.L. 2020-61, Section 102(ii), of the Republic of the Marshall Islands;\n(f) a virtual asset service provider within the meaning of Law No. 14,478/2022 (Brazilian Legal Framework for Crypto-assets) or CVM Resolution No. 175;\n(g) an entity subject to the obligations of FATF Recommendation 15 as a VASP;\n(h) a custodian, depositary, bailee or administrator of digital assets or of third-party financial resources;\n(i) an investment adviser, provider of financial advice or securities analyst.\n\n2.4. Mooze does not exercise custody, possession, discretionary control over balances on behalf of users, ownership, dominion, or the right to use, enjoy or dispose of any digital assets or monetary amounts belonging to the user. The transitory, programmatic and automated processing of digital assets by Mooze's infrastructure during the performance of the Services constitutes technical routing, analogous to the processing of data packets by network equipment (a router), without Mooze acquiring, at any time or in any form, any right, interest or beneficial ownership.\n\n2.5. Mooze does not, under any circumstances, carry out: (i) exchange operations; (ii) conversion between fiat currencies; (iii) conversion between fiat currency and a digital asset, or between digital assets, executed on behalf of the User and in the User's ownership; (iv) financial intermediation; (v) transmission of value on behalf of third parties. Any and all operations involving fiat currency (Brazilian reais) are processed entirely by partners regulated by the Central Bank of Brazil, as described in Section 4. Any and all conversions between digital assets are executed directly by the User, through decentralized peer-to-peer protocols (atomic swap), without Mooze acting as a counterparty.\n\n2.6. Under the Banking (Amendment) Act, 2020 (P.L. 2020-61) of the Republic of the Marshall Islands, Chapter 1, Section 102(ii), the definition of VASP (Virtual Asset Service Provider) covers exclusively natural or legal persons that, as a business, conduct one or more of the following activities \"for or on behalf of another natural or legal person\": (i) exchange between virtual assets and fiat currencies; (ii) exchange between one or more forms of virtual assets; (iii) transfer of virtual assets; (iv) safekeeping and/or administration of virtual assets or of instruments enabling control over virtual assets; (v) participation in and provision of financial services related to an issuer's offer and/or sale of a virtual asset. Mooze does not conduct any of activities (i) through (v) \"for or on behalf of\" third parties, because: (a) it operates exclusively as a non-custodial software provider; (b) it does not hold, and has no technical capacity to hold, the User's private keys; (c) it does not execute conversions on behalf of the User, and limits itself to orchestrating programmatic calls between the User and third-party providers; (d) it does not participate as a counterparty in any transfer or atomic swap.\n\n2.7. Mooze is not subject to the AML Regulations 2002 of the Republic of the Marshall Islands (as amended) as a VASP, because it does not meet the legal criterion of providing services \"for or on behalf of\" third parties. Compliance with anti-money laundering (AML), know-your-customer (KYC) and \"Travel Rule\" obligations relating to transfers above USD 1,000.00 rests exclusively with the Regulated Partners and the other VASPs involved in the operational flow described in Section 4.\n\n2.8. Mooze is an official member of the Liquid Federation (Blockstream), with an active PAK Entry, attesting to its participation in the Liquid Network ecosystem as a technology entity. Participation in the Liquid Federation constitutes a technical and operational relationship, and not a corporate, agency or joint and several liability relationship with Blockstream or with the other members of the federation.",
  "terms_section_3_body": "For purposes of these Terms, the following terms have the meanings indicated:\n\n3.1. \"App\" or \"Mooze Wallet\": self-custodial digital wallet software developed by Mooze, made available for iOS and Android mobile devices (through stores such as Google Play Store, Apple App Store and similar stores, and also through an APK file for direct distribution).\n\n3.2. \"User\": a natural person over 18 (eighteen) years of age with full legal capacity who installs, accesses or uses the App on the User's own initiative.\n\n3.3. \"Self-Custody\": a model in which the User holds exclusive technical control over the User's private keys and seed phrases, without Mooze or any third party having access to, a copy of, knowledge of or the technical capacity to reconstruct such information.\n\n3.4. \"Seed Phrase\": a sequence of 12 (twelve) or 24 (twenty-four) words, generated locally on the User's device in accordance with the open BIP39 standard, which constitutes the sole mechanism for recovering the User's digital wallet.\n\n3.5. \"Liquid Network\": a federated Bitcoin sidechain, developed and maintained by Blockstream and the Liquid Federation, that enables the issuance and transfer of digital assets with Confidential Transactions technology.\n\n3.6. \"DEPIX\": a digital token issued on the Liquid Network by Eulen.app LLC (an entity organized in Saint Kitts and Nevis) in cooperation with the depix.info project, whose value is pegged to the Brazilian real (BRL) at a ratio of 1 (one) DEPIX to R$ 1.00 (one real). As described in the public whitepaper available at depix.info, DEPIX is collateralized partially in fiat currencies and mostly in Bitcoin, through NITI (Non-custodial Interlinked Tokenization Infrastructure) protocols on on-chain networks and on the Liquid Network. Mooze IS NOT the issuer, administrator or guarantor of DEPIX, nor is it responsible for the peg, backing or liquidity of DEPIX.\n\n3.7. \"L-BTC\": the technical representation of Bitcoin on the Liquid Network, issued 1:1 against Bitcoin deposited in the federated peg-in, used for transactions within that network.\n\n3.8. \"Atomic Swap\": a cryptographic mechanism for the direct exchange between two digital assets, executed directly on the blockchain or sidechain, without a custodial intermediary, in which both legs of the transaction are completed simultaneously or neither of them takes effect (all-or-nothing).\n\n3.9. \"SideSwap\": a public, open-source protocol for executing atomic swaps on the Liquid Network.\n\n3.10. \"Confidential Transactions\": a native Liquid Network technology that conceals amounts and asset types in transactions, which are visible only to the parties involved by means of the respective blinding keys.\n\n3.11. \"APP ID\": a technical identifier generated from cryptographic features of the User's device (MediaDRM on Android, DeviceCheck on iOS), resulting in a one-way hash. The APP ID is used exclusively for fraud prevention and control of operational limits, does not allow personal identification of the User and does not constitute personally identifiable data under the LGPD or equivalent legislation.\n\n3.12. \"Regulated Partners\": Brazilian financial and payment institutions, duly authorized and regulated by the Central Bank of Brazil, that participate in the processing of operations involving fiat currency (PIX). These include, without limitation to those listed:\n(a) PLEBIT.COM.BR Soluções em Tecnologia Ltda — CNPJ 43.375.652/0001-13;\n(b) Fits Instituição de Pagamento — CNPJ 13.203.354/0001-85;\n(c) Celcoin — CNPJ 13.935.893/0001-09;\n(d) PLEBZ INTERMEDIACAO DE PAGAMENTOS LTDA — CNPJ 45.808.899/0001-01.\n\n3.13. \"Eulen.app LLC\": a company organized in Saint Kitts and Nevis, issuer of the DEPIX token and responsible for the tokenization technology infrastructure described in its public whitepaper.\n\n3.14. \"PIX\": the instant payment system established, regulated and operated by the Central Bank of Brazil.\n\n3.15. \"Services\": the set of software features made available by Mooze to the User through the App, as described in Section 4.\n\n3.16. \"NITI Protocol\": a decentralized protocol used for the verification and routing of transactions on the Liquid Network.\n\n3.17. \"Blinding Key\": a cryptographic key associated with a Confidential Transaction on the Liquid Network, which allows its holder to view the amounts and asset types transacted in that specific transaction.\n\n3.18. \"MED\" (\"Mecanismo Especial de Devolução\", Special Refund Mechanism): a mechanism established by the Central Bank of Brazil for the refund of amounts in PIX transactions, applicable in cases of fraud or operational failure, governed by the applicable BCB Resolution and operated exclusively by the institutions participating in the PIX arrangement.\n\n3.19. \"Breez\" or \"Breez SDK\": a third-party software development kit (SDK) used by Mooze for technical integration with the Lightning Network.\n\n3.20. \"Hodle\": a third-party service used for complementary features involving the PIX system.\n\n3.21. \"Partner Infratechs\": third-party companies that provide financial technology infrastructure services used by Mooze in the orchestration of its software Services, without providing services directly to the end Users of the App and without any direct contractual relationship with the User.\n\n3.22. \"FATF\": Financial Action Task Force (Grupo de Ação Financeira Internacional), an intergovernmental body referenced in these Terms for purposes of the definition of VASP and the application of Recommendation 15.\n\n3.23. \"Passive Offer\" or \"Reverse Solicitation\": a form of making a service available in which the customer seeks out the provider by the customer's own decision and initiative.",
  "terms_section_4_body": "Mooze makes available to the User, through the App, software services organized into modalities that are independent of one another. Each modality constitutes an autonomous technology service, with a distinct purpose, operation and contractual basis. Use of one modality neither requires nor is a condition for use of the others.\n\n4.1. SERVICE A — SOFTWARE ORCHESTRATION FOR THE ACQUISITION OF DIGITAL TOKENS\n\n4.1.1. Service A consists of Mooze making available a software interface that programmatically orchestrates communication between the User's device, the Regulated Partners and the digital token issuance infrastructure operated by Eulen.app LLC and other Partner Infratechs.\n\n4.1.2. The operational flow of Service A takes place as described below:\n(a) The User, through the App, enters the amount in reais (BRL) that the User wishes to use to acquire DEPIX and generates a PIX QR code, in which, via the User's platform for initiating the operation, the User provides all data necessary for the transaction, which may include public keys, wallet addresses, amounts and general device information;\n(b) The PIX payment is received, processed and settled entirely by one of the Regulated Partners (PLEBIT.COM.BR, Fits Instituição de Pagamento, Celcoin or PLEBZ), which are the only entities authorized to receive and process fiat currency funds in both directions of FIAT transaction flows;\n(c) The Regulated Partner communicates the PIX settlement data to Eulen.app LLC;\n(d) Eulen.app LLC issues the corresponding quantity of DEPIX tokens on the Liquid Network;\n(e) Mooze's software captures the User's wallet address — a public address mathematically derived from the private keys under the User's exclusive control — and transmits that address to the Eulen.app LLC infrastructure so that the DEPIX tokens are delivered directly to the User's Self-Custody address;\n(f) The DEPIX tokens are delivered, through the joint processing system initiated via software with Eulen.app LLC, directly via programmatic routing directed to the User's Self-Custody address on the Liquid Network.\n\n4.1.3. Service A constitutes the provision of software technology services, performed through infrastructure integrated among Mooze, specialized partners and service providers in the ecosystem. Mooze coordinates API (application programming interface) calls between the User's device, the Regulated Partners, Eulen.app LLC and the Partner Infratechs, including the automated verification system described in clause 4.1.4, without acquiring ownership, beneficial possession or control over the routed assets outside predefined programmatic scopes.\n\n4.1.4. The processing of digital assets under Service A involves multiple layers of technical and operational verification performed by integrated systems of specialized partners and service providers. Completion of processing may result from joint review procedures that, depending on the nature and characteristics of the operation, are governed by the following characteristics:\n(a) Processing is governed by integrated automated systems, whose criteria are determined by participants in the technology ecosystem; the possible outcomes are: (i) completion of the operation, with delivery of the assets to the User's Self-Custody address; or (ii) reversal of the operation, with return of the assets to Eulen.app LLC and notice of the PIX payment chargeback to the Regulated Partners;\n(b) there are no alternative technical destinations for the assets other than those described in (a)(i) and (a)(ii) — the structure of the system does not allow for deviations;\n(c) the integrated automated systems do not allow for discretionary intervention in individual operations;\n(d) Mooze does not acquire, at any time, beneficial ownership, any property right, or any right to use, enjoy or dispose of the tokens in transit;\n(e) the tokens in transit are not commingled with Mooze's assets, nor used as backing, collateral or reserve for any obligation of Mooze;\n(f) the delivery operation constitutes an atomic handoff: until the moment immediately prior to release to the User, the tokens remain under programmatic technical control with a destination predefined for the operation itself;\n(g) technical maintenance of the anti-fraud system (correction of defects, updating of programmatic rules, calibration of thresholds) constitutes software development and does not amount to discretionary intervention in individual operations.\n\n4.1.5. Operations under Service A may be subject to verification procedures performed by integrated automated systems of partners in the technology ecosystem. The duration and methodology of the verification procedures are determined by these automated systems, and may result in immediate processing or in additional review for a variable period depending on the nature and characteristics of the operation. During processing:\n(a) the assets remain in automated transit, without commingling with assets of other operations and without fungibility with Mooze's assets;\n(b) Mooze does not, and cannot, exercise any use, enjoyment, lending, investment, rehypothecation or any form of economic exploitation of the tokens in transition;\n(c) once the verification period expires without any inconsistency being flagged, the assets are automatically released to the User's Self-Custody address;\n(d) the transitory processing does not constitute custody, safekeeping, deposit or administration of assets on behalf of the User, because (i) it does not arise from a safekeeping or deposit agreement with the User, but from a technical procedure of the ecosystem applied via the processing route for delivery, and (ii) at no time does Mooze acquire beneficial ownership of or discretionary power over the assets.\n\n4.1.6. Operations may be reversed when integrated automated systems or Regulated Partners detect risk flags, technical inconsistencies or applicable regulatory requirements (including MED). In that case, the digital assets are reversed to Eulen.app LLC via blockchain within the processing time of the respective networks used. Processing of the chargeback of the PIX payment in fiat currency is the exclusive responsibility of the Regulated Partners, under the jurisdiction and regulation of the Central Bank of Brazil, and may take up to 7 (seven) calendar days counted on average from the start of the operation. The additional period between the reversal of the tokens to Eulen.app LLC and the completion of the PIX chargeback refers exclusively to the processing time of the Brazilian banking system by the Regulated Partners, during which period Mooze does not hold any tokens or financial resources related to the operation.\n\n4.1.7. Processing of the PIX payment, including verification of the payer's identity (KYC), anti-money laundering (AML), compliance with the \"Travel Rule\" in cross-border transfers of virtual assets upon events triggered by regulated amount thresholds, and other regulatory obligations before the Central Bank of Brazil, the Council for Financial Activities Control (COAF) and the Brazilian Federal Revenue Service, is the exclusive responsibility of the Regulated Partners and the other VASPs involved, within the limits of their respective activities.\n\n4.1.8. The issuance of DEPIX tokens is the exclusive responsibility of Eulen.app LLC and the depix.info project, which operate independently of Mooze. Mooze does not guarantee the peg, liquidity, backing, solvency or continuity of operation of DEPIX, nor does Mooze represent or answer for operations related to DEPIX, Eulen.app LLC and its contractual partnerships.\n\n4.1.9. Service A constitutes the provision of a software service (SaaS) and does not amount to: (a) a financial service; (b) an exchange operation; (c) financial intermediation; (d) transmission of value; (e) the provision of virtual asset services (VASP) within the meaning of the Banking (Amendment) Act, 2020 (RMI) or of regulatory laws of Brazilian territory; (f) any activity subject to financial, banking or insurance regulation.\n\n4.2. SERVICE B — INTERFACE FOR A DECENTRALIZED PROTOCOL FOR CONVERSION BETWEEN DIGITAL UNITS\n\n4.2.1. Service B consists of Mooze making available a software interface that allows the User to interact with the SideSwap protocol to execute atomic swaps between digital assets on the Liquid Network, as well as, where applicable, with the Breez SDK for access to the Lightning Network.\n\n4.2.2. Service B is entirely independent of Service A. Use of one Service neither implies nor requires use of the other.\n\n4.2.3. The operational flow of Service B takes place as described below:\n(a) The User, from the User's self-custodial wallet in the App, voluntarily initiates a request for conversion between digital assets (for example, DEPIX to L-BTC);\n(b) Mooze's software presents the User with a graphical interface for interacting with the SideSwap protocol (or the Breez SDK, where applicable);\n(c) The atomic swap is executed directly on the Liquid Network (or on the Lightning Network, where applicable), through the corresponding protocol, between the User and the liquidity available in the protocol;\n(d) Mooze does not participate as a counterparty, custodian, market maker or liquidity provider at any stage of the atomic swap;\n(e) The conversion takes place peer-to-peer, directly on the blockchain or sidechain, cryptographically guaranteed by the atomic swap mechanism — at no time is there an intermediary holding both sides of the operation.\n\n4.2.4. Mooze's role in Service B is analogous to that of a web browser that provides access to a website: Mooze provides the software interface for the User to interact with a decentralized protocol, without participating in the execution of the protocol itself.\n\n4.2.5. The SideSwap protocol is public, open source and operates in a decentralized manner on the Liquid Network. The Breez SDK is public third-party software used for access to the Lightning Network. Mooze does not control, operate, administer, govern or maintain any of these protocols or SDKs.\n\n4.2.6. Service B does not constitute brokerage, exchange, financial intermediation, foreign exchange, trading, market making or asset settlement activity. It constitutes exclusively the provision of a software interface for access to decentralized protocols.\n\n4.2.7. Mooze does not guarantee: (a) the availability of liquidity in the protocols used; (b) the successful execution of atomic swaps; (c) the conversion rates charged by the protocols; (d) the operational continuity of third-party protocols or SDKs.\n\n4.2.8. For access to the Lightning Network, Mooze makes available the technical integration with the public Breez SDK, subject to the same terms described herein for SideSwap.\n\n4.2.9. When the User selects, by the User's own voluntary decision, a final digital asset other than DEPIX (for example, L-BTC), Mooze's software sequentially orchestrates the execution of Service A (acquisition of DEPIX) followed by Service B (conversion of DEPIX into the selected asset via the decentralized Sideswap protocol). The conversion is executed entirely by the decentralized protocol. Mooze limits itself to orchestrating the software calls necessary for the final asset to be available via the User's Self-Custody address. The User acknowledges that this sequential orchestration constitutes the provision of an automated software service (SaaS) and does not amount to foreign exchange activity for which Mooze is responsible, brokerage, financial intermediation or VASP activity, because it is executed exclusively via the Sideswap protocol.\n\n4.3. MERCHANT MODE\n\n4.3.1. The App provides a feature called \"Merchant Mode\", which allows the User to receive payments via PIX directly into the User's self-custodial wallet in the App, both from third-party payers and in the form of self-payments.\n\n4.3.2. Merchant Mode uses the same technology infrastructure described in Service A (clause 4.1), and the same provisions regarding the nature of the service, the responsibilities of the Regulated Partners and the absence of custody by Mooze apply in full.\n\n4.3.3. Merchant Mode constitutes a software feature and does not amount to an acquiring, sub-acquiring or merchant accreditation service, a payment arrangement, a payment gateway or any regulated financial service. The PIX payment QR code is generated by the Merchant-User itself through the App, using the infrastructure of the Regulated Partners. Mooze does not participate in, intermediate, know of, validate or endorse the underlying commercial relationship between the Merchant-User and the payer. The payer makes a conventional PIX payment to the Regulated Partner, without any interaction, contractual relationship or direct communication with Mooze.\n\n4.3.4. Payments received through Merchant Mode are subject to verification procedures performed by integrated systems of partners and service providers. Completion of processing may take variable periods, from minutes to several days, according to the applicable procedures determined by each participant in the processing chain.\n\n4.3.5. Payments may be reversed when integrated review systems detect technical inconsistencies, regulatory requirements or other conditions that result in non-completion of the operation. The reversal will be processed by the service providers responsible for the original flow. A User who uses Merchant Mode MUST NOT deliver a product or service to the payer before final confirmation of the payment through the tracking features available in the App.\n\n4.3.6. Any losses, damages or disputes arising from the delivery of a product or service before final confirmation of the processing of the payment are the exclusive responsibility of the Merchant-User, and no liability falls on Mooze, the Regulated Partners or the Partner Infratechs.\n\n4.3.7. A User who uses Merchant Mode assumes full civil, tax and criminal responsibility for the operations carried out through the App, including operations carried out by third parties who use the device under the User's physical custody.\n\n4.3.8. Operational questions about payments should be directed to Mooze support at suporte@mooze.app.\n\n4.4. NATURE OF THE INTEGRATED TECHNOLOGY ECOSYSTEM\n\n4.4.1. The Services made available by Mooze operate in a complex technology ecosystem involving multiple service providers, third-party infrastructures, decentralized protocols and integrated systems.\n\n4.4.2. The execution of operations under the Services involves, on a non-exhaustive basis: (a) software infrastructure developed by Mooze; (b) systems of specialized partners and providers; (c) infrastructures of the Regulated Partners; (d) public blockchain protocols; (e) review and verification systems operated jointly by participants in the ecosystem.\n\n4.4.3. Mooze does not have exclusive control over all of the components, systems and processes involved in the execution of the Services. Decisions on the processing, approval, timing, reversal or non-performance of operations may result from automated systems, third-party procedures, regulatory requirements or technical conditions applied by any participant in the ecosystem.\n\n4.4.4. The User acknowledges that the provision of the Services constitutes technological coordination among multiple agents, and does not amount to a unilateral relationship or a service provided exclusively by Mooze. Mooze acts as a provider of software integration components within a broader ecosystem.",
  "terms_section_5_body": "5.1. The App operates under a full Self-Custody model. Private keys and seed phrases are generated and stored exclusively on the User's device and are technically inaccessible to Mooze.\n\n5.2. Mooze does not have, at any time and under any circumstances, access to, knowledge of, possession of, control over, a copy or backup of, custody of, or the technical capacity to reconstruct the User's private keys, seed phrases or passwords.\n\n5.3. The User is solely and exclusively responsible for the safekeeping, security and integrity of the User's private keys, seed phrases and passwords. Loss of these elements results in the permanent and irreversible loss of access to the digital assets stored in the wallet.\n\n5.4. Mooze does not have the technical capacity to recover, restore, access, transfer or recreate the User's digital assets in the event of loss of the private keys or seed phrases. Requests to that effect are technically impossible to fulfill.\n\n5.5. The User's wallet addresses and public keys are mathematically derived from the User's private keys by means of a deterministic cryptographic algorithm. Mooze uses this data exclusively as a technical parameter for automated routing during the performance of the Services, transmitting it via infrastructure for the direct delivery of the assets to the User.\n\n5.6. The User acknowledges that Self-Custody is the structural pillar of Mooze's model and a determining element of its legal classification as a non-VASP. Any attempt to circumvent the Self-Custody model (for example, demanding that Mooze safekeep keys, hold assets in custody or carry out the discretionary recovery of seed phrases) is incompatible with the nature of the Service, will not be fulfilled.",
  "terms_section_6_body": "6.1. SAFEKEEPING OF PASSWORDS AND SEED PHRASES\n\n6.1.1. The User is fully and exclusively responsible for the creation, storage and protection of the User's passwords, private keys and seed phrases.\n\n6.1.2. The User must store the User's seed phrase in a secure location, preferably offline (on a physical medium such as paper, engraved steel or a dedicated device), and never share it with third parties, including Mooze or any person who claims to be a representative of Mooze.\n\n6.1.3. Mooze NEVER asks the User, through any means of communication (e-mail, Telegram, telephone, social media, advertisements, in-app chat), for the User's private keys, seed phrases or passwords. Any request to that effect must be considered a fraud attempt and reported to official support at suporte@mooze.app.\n\n6.1.4. The user is solely responsible for verifying legitimacy in cases of communications or phishing attempts, or communications via homograph channels impersonating Mooze; with this knowledge provided through these terms, it is advised that, for communications from a homograph or suspicious domain similar to that of Mooze, the user should make contact by forwarding the suspicious contacts or messages (see section 6.1.3.) to suporte@mooze.app for assistance and verification; Mooze communicates with customers exclusively via the mooze.app domain.\n\n6.2. CONSEQUENCES OF LOSS OF ACCESS\n\n6.2.1. Loss of the seed phrase results in the permanent and irreversible loss of access to all digital assets stored in the associated wallet.\n\n6.2.2. Mooze cannot restore, recover or recreate access to the User's wallet in the event of loss of the seed phrase.\n\n6.2.3. The User acknowledges and accepts that Self-Custody entails full and exclusive responsibility for the User's digital assets, including the risk of total and definitive loss due to the User's own act or omission and lack of skill with respect to Blockchain and cryptocurrency technologies.\n\n6.2.4. The user, upon uninstalling the Mooze application, rotating data via platforms for access to the services via Mooze, or rotating wallets or seed phrases on the same device or on different devices, is aware of the possibility of data loss, such as storage of blockchain histories, histories of payments via partner processors, possible loss of standing in internal user reputation scores via Mooze systems and services (score and transaction limit related to banking transactions via regulated partners), and any data, not limited to these, that is saved locally for privacy and security; these actions may result in these consequences, and the user hereby declares that the user is fully aware of the consequences of these actions.\n\n6.3. DEVICE SECURITY AND SOURCE FROM WHICH THE SERVICES ARE OBTAINED\n\n6.3.1. The User is responsible for the security of the mobile device used to access the App, including: (a) keeping the operating system up to date; (b) using biometric authentication or a strong device password; (c) protection against malware and applications from untrusted sources; (d) refraining from rooting, jailbreaking or using emulators; the user may download the application via official authorized stores under Mooze's identification or through sources such as its official Github (github.com/mooze-labs), both of which sources offer ways to verify the authenticity of the source of services and applications, such as verification of the authenticity of the application and its integrity via hash ID checks in the public repositories; Mooze is not responsible for any problem arising from users who use tampered and/or fraudulent application download sources or service sources, nor for losses arising from failure to verify the source of services or of the applications obtained; the user hereby consents that the user may use verification via Mooze's official Github and the secure security methods of the available official stores.\n\n6.3.2. Mooze is not responsible for losses arising from compromise of the User's device, including malware infection, unauthorized access to the device, interception of data by third parties or use of modified devices.",
  "terms_section_7_body": "7.1. Use of the Services is subject to processing and technology fees (the \"Service Fee\" or \"Software Service Fee\") charged by reason of the operation of the technology ecosystem described in Section 4.\n\n7.2. The Service Fees compensate the technology infrastructure providers involved in the operation, including but not limited to: software development and maintenance, systems integration, processing of operations, network infrastructure, security and other technical services necessary for the functioning of the ecosystem.\n\n7.3. The Software Service Fee is calculated as a percentage of the amount of the operation and deducted from the amount of digital assets delivered to the User. The current percentage is displayed to the User on the operation confirmation screen, before the operation is carried out, and is also disclosed in the informational menus of the App.\n\n7.4. Mooze reserves the right to change the Software Service Fee percentages at any time, by means of an update in the App or due to needs for reference pegging to Bitcoin quotes (example: Bitcoin Liquid network fees and similar Bitcoin-denominated references may be adjusted due to fluctuating quotes). Continued use of the App after the change constitutes acceptance of the new percentages or of the needs for non-fixed reference amounts.\n\n7.5. The Software Service Fee constitutes compensation for a software service (SaaS), analogous in nature to the fees charged by technology platforms for the use of their services. It does not constitute a financial fee, brokerage commission, foreign exchange fee, foreign exchange spread or financial charge of any kind.\n\n7.6. The Regulated Partners, the decentralized protocols (SideSwap, Breez, Lightning) and the Partner Infratechs may apply their own fees, spreads, charges or network costs, independent of Mooze's Software Service Fee, over which Mooze exercises no control and bears no responsibility. Mooze informs the User of these pass-through charges on the operation confirmation screen, on a fixed or floating basis, on the platform used.\n\n7.7. Mining costs and network fees relating to transactions on the Bitcoin, Liquid Network or Lightning Network networks are the responsibility of the User and are independent of the Software Service Fee. Network fees incurred during the performance of the Services by the Regulated Partners, Partner Infratechs or protocols used may be passed on to the User, in addition to the Software Service Fee, as displayed on the confirmation screen before the operation is carried out.",
  "terms_section_8_body": "8.1. The reference values displayed in the App for digital assets (Bitcoin, L-BTC, DEPIX, L-USDT and others) are obtained from public market sources and serve exclusively as an informational reference.\n\n8.2. Mooze does not guarantee the accuracy, precision or real-time updating of the prices displayed. Price variation between the time of display and the time an operation is carried out is inherent to the functioning of digital asset markets.\n\n8.3. The display of prices in the App: (a) does not constitute an offer, public offering, recommendation, investment advice, securities analysis or guarantee of value; (b) does not amount to a public offering of securities within the meaning of Law No. 6,385/76 or equivalent legislation; (c) does not qualify as \"investment advice\" or \"solicitation\" within the meaning of the regulations of the United States, the European Union, the United Kingdom or any other jurisdiction.\n\n8.4. The User acknowledges that digital assets are subject to high volatility and that the User may suffer significant losses in value. Mooze is not responsible for losses arising from price variation.",
  "terms_section_9_body": "9.1. Mooze provides the App and the Services \"as is\" and \"as available\", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including, without limitation, warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement.\n\n9.2. Mooze shall not be liable for:\n(a) losses of digital assets arising from the loss, compromise or misuse of private keys, seed phrases or passwords by the User;\n(b) losses arising from compromise of the User's device and use of a fake Platform (homograph / fake domain) or of an application that is tampered with or downloaded from an unofficial source;\n(c) unavailability, failures, delays, forks, reorganizations or interruptions on the Liquid Network, the Bitcoin network, the Lightning Network or any other blockchain or sidechain network;\n(d) failures, unavailability or delays in the services provided by the Regulated Partners, Eulen.app LLC, the depix.info project, the SideSwap protocol, the Breez SDK or any third-party infrastructure providers;\n(e) acts of fraud, phishing, social engineering, SIM swap or any form of attack directed at the User by third parties (including obtaining a fraudulent application or software service that the user consented to use without verifying the source, as discussed in item 6.3), including through deceptive communications, use of homograph e-mail contacts, domains similar to Mooze's official domain, tampered applications, fake profiles on social media or messaging apps, and any other forms of attack directed at the User, the prevention of which is not under Mooze's control;\n(f) errors in the entry of wallet addresses by the User, resulting in digital assets being sent to incorrect addresses; failures in sending or receiving assets on third-party platforms and services; refusal of assets by third-party services; failures of smart contracts on any blockchain networks initiated directly or indirectly by the User through the User's Self-Custody; use of insufficient network fees that result in the transaction not being mined or being delayed; use of the Services via PIX, by third parties, for willful or unlawful activities, notwithstanding the existence of joint anti-fraud systems — cases in which Mooze is not responsible, because it does not intermediate, endorse or validate the underlying relationship between the Merchant-User and the payer;\n(g) regulatory changes that affect the availability of the Services in a given jurisdiction, including total interruption or discontinuation in response to supervening legal requirements;\n(h) variation in the value of digital assets;\n(i) investment decisions made by the User based on information displayed in the App or in any other Mooze material;\n(j) indirect, incidental, consequential or punitive damages, lost profits, loss of opportunity, loss of data or reputational loss.\n\n9.2.1. Mooze is not responsible for: (i) decisions made by automated programmatic systems participating in the ecosystem; (ii) processing times determined by third-party infrastructures or Regulated Partners; (iii) review criteria applied by specialized service providers; (iv) reversals requested by financial institutions, Regulated Partners or regulatory authorities.\n\n9.3. Mooze is not responsible for any tax, fiscal, regulatory, labor or legal obligations of the User arising from the holding, use, conversion, disposal, receipt or movement of digital assets. Responsibility for compliance with tax obligations — including, where applicable, any normative instructions or ancillary obligations related to crypto-assets and/or income tax returns under the laws of the User's tax residence — rests entirely with the User, including the responsibility to monitor the User's own onchain transactions in order to comply with obligations of a personal and individual nature.\n\n9.4. The App may operate in a BETA version, which may coexist with stable release versions for a fixed period. The User agrees that, during the BETA period, defects, instabilities or interruptions may occur, and accepts all resulting risks.\n\n9.5. The seed phrases generated in the App are compatible with the open BIP39 standard and with the Liquid Network. In the event of critical unavailability of the App, discontinuation of the Services or the winding up of Mooze's activities, the User may recover access to the User's digital assets by importing the User's seed phrases into any wallet software compatible with the corresponding network (for example, the Blockstream App for the Liquid Network and the onchain Bitcoin network, which automatically derives all balances held by the user and their blockchain histories). This provision constitutes a structural guarantee of Self-Custody and an integral element of Mooze's non-custodial model.",
  "terms_section_10_body": "10.1. Mooze implements software-level security mechanisms for fraud prevention, including:\n(a) linking of the APP ID (technical device identifier) to the operations carried out;\n(b) a scoring system by risk levels;\n(c) progressive limits per operation according to the history of the APP ID;\n(d) detection of anomalous patterns (smurfing, bursting, coordinated self-payments, use of multiple devices for the same operation, use of emulators, use of modified devices).\n\n10.2. Mooze's anti-fraud measures are exclusively technological in nature, applied to the software flow, and do not replace the anti-money laundering (AML), customer identification (KYC) and \"Travel Rule\" obligations of the Regulated Partners and the other VASPs involved.\n\n10.3. The Regulated Partners are solely responsible for compliance with AML and KYC obligations before the Central Bank of Brazil, COAF and other competent authorities, under Law No. 9,613/1998, Law No. 14,478/2022 and applicable regulations or other future laws that may become ancillary.",
  "terms_section_11_body": "11.1. Mooze reserves the right to suspend, limit or terminate an APP ID's access to the Services, with or without prior notice, in the following cases:\n(a) detection of a pattern indicative of fraud, unlawful activity or attempted abuse of the Services;\n(b) use of compromised, rooted or jailbroken devices, emulators or manipulation tools;\n(c) attempts to circumvent the security mechanisms, anti-fraud mechanisms or operational limits of the App, attempted sabotage or attacks on Mooze infrastructure;\n(d) patterns indicative of use of the Services for money laundering, terrorist financing, sanctions evasion or any unlawful purpose;\n(e) a substantiated request from a competent authority or a valid court order;\n(f) use from a restricted jurisdiction under clause 12.1(a).\n\n11.2. Suspension of access affects exclusively the ability of the APP ID to initiate new operations that use connections to the PIX system of the regulated partners through the App. The digital assets in the User's Self-Custody remain entirely under the User's control, because they are stored in the User's own wallet and are accessible by means of the User's seed phrase in any wallet software compatible with the corresponding network.\n\n11.3. Mooze will cooperate with competent authorities upon a valid court order, subject to the technical limitations inherent to the self-custodial model (Mooze has no access to the User's private keys, seed phrases or digital assets). Mooze's cooperation is limited to providing the data actually in its technical possession (APP ID, public addresses, transaction data, blinding keys), under Section 5 of the Privacy Policy.\n\n11.4. MED procedures are processed by the Regulated Partners, which are entities participating in the PIX system. Mooze collaborates technologically with the Regulated Partners, providing APP ID information and transaction data when requested, but does not operate as a participant in the PIX system.",
  "terms_section_12_body": "12.1. The User expressly and knowingly represents, warrants and undertakes that:\n(a) the User uses the Services in compliance with the legislation applicable in the User's jurisdiction of domicile and residence. The User represents that the User is not a resident, domiciliary, citizen or national of, or a \"US Person\" within the meaning of Regulation S (SEC), nor a resident, national or citizen of: (i) the United States of America and its territories; (ii) the United Kingdom; (iii) the Member States of the European Union and of the European Economic Area; (iv) jurisdictions included in the sanctions lists of OFAC (U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control), the sanctions of the United Nations Security Council, or the sanctions of the European Union or the United Kingdom; (v) jurisdictions classified by the FATF as High-Risk Jurisdictions Subject to a Call for Action; Mooze may use means of regional verification to carry out such checks, of which the user is aware and to which the user agrees. If it is found, at any time, that the User is a resident, national or citizen of a restricted jurisdiction, the APP ID's access to the Services may be immediately suspended or terminated. This clause does not, under any circumstances, extend regulatory jurisdiction over Mooze Labs LLC with respect to such jurisdictions, and has effect solely as a contractual filter;\n(b) the funds used in operations via PIX are of lawful and provable origin, arising from lawfully conducted activities;\n(c) the User does not use the Services for money laundering, terrorist financing, tax evasion, sanctions evasion, human trafficking, drug trafficking, corruption or any unlawful purpose;\n(d) the User is solely responsible for reporting and paying taxes levied on the holding, use, receipt, conversion or disposal of digital assets in the User's jurisdiction, including, where applicable, compliance with the national Normative Instructions relating to the User's current tax residence or citizenship.\n(e) the User must use the Services only with knowledge of the crypto-asset regulatory obligations of the User's tax residence or nationality, and acknowledges that Mooze does not qualify as a virtual asset service provider (PSAV, virtual asset service provider) within the meaning of the aforementioned law, because (i) it does not carry out custody, intermediation, administration, trading or brokerage of virtual assets in the name or on behalf of third parties, (ii) it operates exclusively as a non-custodial software provider, (iii) it is headquartered outside Brazilian territory, in a foreign jurisdiction;\n(f) the User understands and accepts that the User obtained access to the Services through the User's own active and voluntary search (reverse solicitation), without having been the object of coercion or linguistic persuasion of any kind initiated by Mooze;\n(g) the User understands and accepts the risks inherent to blockchain technology, including volatility, regulatory risk, fork risk, technological risk and risk of total loss.\n\n12.2. Mooze does not provide tax, fiscal or legal advisory services. The User must seek independent professional advice for compliance with the User's legal obligations.\n\n12.3. Mooze does not file, on behalf of the User, tax returns, operation reports, income statements or communications to any tax authority. The User is solely responsible for such obligations.\n\n12.4. Mooze does not provide Services to politically exposed persons (PEPs) subject to specific restrictions of sanctioning jurisdictions, and the User must properly declare the User's status and refrain from using the Services in violation of such restrictions.",
  "terms_section_13_body": "13.1. These Terms are governed exclusively by the laws of the Republic of the Marshall Islands, including, in particular, the Associations Law (Title 52, MIRC) and the Banking (Amendment) Act, 2020 (P.L. 2020-61).\n\n13.2. Mooze Labs LLC is an entity duly organized in the Republic of the Marshall Islands and operates from that jurisdiction. Mooze DOES NOT have a permanent establishment, subsidiary, branch, representative office, agency, agent or any form of physical, operational or legal presence in Brazil or in any other jurisdiction, other than the jurisdiction of organization.\n\n13.3. The relationship between Mooze and the Regulated Partners is governed by independent international contracts, which do not create any corporate relationship, representation, agency, mandate, appointment of an agent, consortium or joint and several liability between Mooze and such partners.\n\n13.4. Any use of the Services by a User domiciled in Brazil does not, by itself, imply submission of Mooze to Brazilian jurisdiction, by reason of the Passive Offer nature and the absence of an establishment in the country, subject to the limits of applicable mandatory laws.",
  "terms_section_14_body": "14.1. Any dispute, controversy or claim arising out of or relating to these Terms shall be resolved, at Mooze's sole discretion:\n(a) by the competent courts of the Republic of the Marshall Islands; or\n(b) by international arbitration conducted under the UNCITRAL Arbitration Rules (United Nations Commission on International Trade Law), by a sole arbitrator, in the English language, with the seat of arbitration to be determined by Mooze.\n\n14.2. The User waives any forum other than those indicated in clause 14.1, except where such waiver is prohibited by the mandatory law of the User's jurisdiction of domicile.\n\n14.3. Before initiating any formal proceeding, the User must send a written notice to Mooze containing the complete data obtained from the Mooze application or Platform, through the channel indicated in Section 19, describing the matter in detail. The parties will use good-faith efforts to reach an amicable resolution within 30 (thirty) calendar days from receipt of the notice.\n\n14.4. In the event of arbitration, each party will bear its own costs and fees, and the administrative costs of the arbitration will be borne by the losing party, to the extent permitted by the UNCITRAL Rules.",
  "terms_section_15_body": "15.1. All software, source code, design, graphical interface, trademarks, logos, trade names, editorial content and documentation of the App are the exclusive property of Mooze Labs LLC or its licensors, except where expressly made available as open source in an official Mooze repository on GitHub. Whatever is not expressly made available as open source remains protected by applicable intellectual property law.\n\n15.2. Use of the App does not confer on the User any intellectual property right in the App or its components, except for the limited personal use rights arising from these Terms.\n\n15.3. Reproduction, modification, distribution, reverse engineering, decompilation, disassembly or creation of derivative works of the App is prohibited without the express written authorization of Mooze, except for what is expressly made available as open source in Mooze's official repository and used under the terms of the license indicated there.\n\n15.4. The source code of the App is publicly available at https://github.com/mooze-labs/mooze-client under the terms of the license indicated there. Use of the source code is subject exclusively to the terms of that license, independently of these Terms.",
  "terms_section_16_body": "16.1. ENTIRE AGREEMENT\nThese Terms, together with the accompanying Privacy Policy, constitute the entire agreement between Mooze and the User with respect to the subject matter hereof, superseding any prior agreements, understandings, memoranda or communications, whether oral or written.\n\n16.2. SEVERABILITY\nIf any provision of these Terms is declared invalid, void, unlawful or unenforceable by a competent court or arbitrator, the remaining provisions will remain in full force and effect. The invalid provision will be interpreted and, where possible, replaced by a valid provision that most closely approximates the original intention of the parties and the economic and legal balance of the contract.\n\n16.3. WAIVER\nMooze's failure or forbearance to require compliance with any provision of these Terms, on one or more occasions, will not constitute a waiver of the right to require it subsequently.\n\n16.4. ASSIGNMENT\nThe User may not assign, transfer, sublicense or encumber the User's rights or obligations under these Terms without the prior written authorization of Mooze. Mooze may freely assign its rights and obligations under these Terms to any affiliate, successor, acquirer or assignee, upon notice to the User through the official channels.\n\n16.5. FORCE MAJEURE AND SUPERVENING ILLEGALITY\nMooze will not be liable for any delay or impossibility in the performance of its obligations arising from events beyond its reasonable control, including, without limitation:\n(a) failures or interruptions on the Liquid Network, the Bitcoin network, the Lightning Network or any blockchain network;\n(b) unavailability of the services of the Regulated Partners or of third-party infrastructure providers;\n(c) cyberattacks, or failures of internet or telecommunications infrastructure;\n(d) governmental, regulatory or judicial decisions, in any jurisdiction, that restrict the operation or render it unfeasible;\n(e) natural disasters, pandemics, wars, strikes, civil unrest or states of emergency;\n(f) legislative or regulatory changes that make the provision of the Services unlawful or unfeasible in a given jurisdiction, in which case Mooze may suspend or terminate the Services in the respective jurisdiction without additional liability, subject to the Self-Custody of the User's assets.\n\n16.6. INDEMNIFICATION\nThe User agrees to indemnify, defend and hold harmless Mooze, its affiliates, directors, members, employees, contractors, agents and licensors from and against any claims, damages, losses, costs (including reasonable attorneys' fees) and liabilities arising from:\n(a) use of the Services by the User in breach of these Terms;\n(b) violation of any applicable law or regulation by the User;\n(c) third-party claims related to acts or omissions of the User;\n(d) provision of false, inaccurate or incomplete information by the User, including false representations regarding non-residence in restricted jurisdictions and regarding the lawful origin of funds.\n\n16.7. DISTRIBUTION OF THE APP\nDistribution of the App on digital platforms, including Google Play Store, Apple App Store and other channels, is carried out jointly by Mooze LLC, a limited liability company organized in the State of Delaware, United States, in its capacity as authorized distributor of Mooze Labs LLC, under an independent distribution agreement entered into between the parties. Mooze LLC (Delaware) acts exclusively as distributor and representative for purposes of publication on digital platforms, without assuming any responsibilities for development, operation, user support, regulatory compliance or custody of assets. Ownership, development, operation and all legal, regulatory and contractual responsibilities relating to the App and the Services remain exclusively with Mooze Labs LLC (Republic of the Marshall Islands). The relationship between Mooze Labs LLC and Mooze LLC (Delaware) does not change the legal nature, regulatory classification, applicable jurisdiction or any provisions of these Terms. Compliance with the distribution policies of the app stores (including, without limitation, the Cryptocurrency Exchanges and Software Wallets policy — Google Play and App Store Review Guidelines 3.1.5 — Apple) is achieved by means of a declaration that Mooze Wallet is an exclusively non-custodial wallet, outside the scope that requires a VASP license for publication.\n\n16.8. LANGUAGE\nThese Terms are originally drafted in Brazilian Portuguese. In the event of translations into other languages, the Portuguese version prevails in case of any divergence of interpretation; all of the terms drafted and presented herein, mainly in Brazilian Portuguese, exist for the sole and exclusive purpose of providing clarification to the regional LATAM public, the main region where Brazil's PIX services have the greatest reach, and this communication fact shall not be interpreted as an intention to establish a seat in and/or perform software services in territories beyond the place of organization of Mooze Labs LLC.",
  "terms_section_17_body": "17.1. The App and the Services are intended exclusively for natural persons aged 18 (eighteen) years or older.\n\n17.2. By using the App, the User represents that the User is at least 18 (eighteen) years of age and has full legal capacity to enter into binding contracts.\n\n17.3. Mooze reserves the right to suspend or terminate the access of any User who is found to be an unemancipated minor under 18 (eighteen) years of age.\n\n17.4. The App constitutes exclusively software for the management of a self-custodial digital wallet and the instrumentation of financial operations with digital assets, and does not amount to a social network, social media platform, messaging service, streaming platform, entertainment service, electronic game application or any form of digital platform with features for engagement or social interaction among users.\n\nBy reason of this nature, Mooze does not fall within the scope of application of Law No. 15,211/2025 (Law for the Protection of Children and Adolescents in the Digital Environment — \"ECA Digital\"), whose obligations are directed at social networks, entertainment platforms, electronic games and services with addictive or behavioral engagement features. Mooze does not make available, and does not have the technical capacity to make available:\n\n(a) features for creating, publishing or sharing content among users;\n(b) social interaction mechanisms (likes, comments, reactions, shares);\n(c) networks of contacts, followers, friendships or connections among users;\n(d) content recommendation algorithms, personalized feeds or infinite scroll;\n(e) chat, messaging, or direct or indirect communication among users of the App;\n(f) public user profiles, timelines or spaces for user-generated content;\n(g) gamification mechanisms, engagement rewards, behavioral notifications or features designed to maximize usage time.\n\nUse of the Services by Brazilians presupposes, structurally and unavoidably, the User's full legal capacity, under articles 3, 4 and 5 of Law No. 10,406/2002 (Brazilian Civil Code), because the Services involve entering into binding contracts and disposing of financial assets — legal acts that unemancipated minors are legally unable to perform on their own. This structural requirement constitutes, by itself, a legal mechanism for excluding children and adolescents that is incompatible with any classification as a digital platform subject to the obligations of Law No. 15,211/2025 or to the provisions of the Statute of Children and Adolescents (Law No. 8,069/1990) applicable to entertainment and content services.",
  "terms_section_18_body": "18.1. Mooze reserves the right to change these Terms at any time by publishing the updated version in the App and at https://mooze.app/termosdeuso/, with an indication of the date of the new version.\n\n18.2. Material changes will be communicated to the User through the App, the Telegram support channel or by e-mail, when available.\n\n18.3. Continued use of the App after the publication of changes constitutes tacit acceptance of the updated Terms.\n\n18.4. A User who does not agree with the changes must cease using the App. The digital assets in the User's Self-Custody remain under the User's exclusive control and are accessible by means of the User's seed phrase in any compatible wallet software.",
  "terms_section_19_body": "19.1. For questions, requests or communications related to these Terms, the User may contact Mooze through the following official channels:\n(a) Support e-mail: suporte@mooze.app\n(b) Telegram support channel: https://t.me/+zkNS6KIDsEcyZDkx (also accessible via https://moozeapp.keepo.bio)\n(c) Automated FAQ via Telegram\n\n19.2. Formal notices of a legal nature (including dispute notices under clause 14.3, subpoenas, service of process or court orders) must be addressed in writing to Mooze Labs LLC, Trust Company Complex, Ajeltake Island, Ajeltake Road, Majuro, Marshall Islands MH96960, Republic of the Marshall Islands, with a copy to the e-mail suporte@mooze.app; delivery through any other channels or jurisdictions does not constitute valid service of process.\n\n19.3. Mooze will use efforts to respond to support communications within 2 (two) to 10 (ten) business days. Formal notices will be answered within the time limits applicable under RMI law or UNCITRAL arbitration, as the case may be.",
  "privacy_section_header_body": "Last updated: 04/18/2026\n\nMooze Labs LLC\nRepublic of the Marshall Islands\nhttps://mooze.app",
  "privacy_section_1_body": "1.1. Mooze Labs LLC (\"Mooze\"), a company duly organized in the Republic of the Marshall Islands, is committed to protecting privacy and to minimizing personal data in the use of the Mooze Wallet application (the \"App\").\n\n1.2. This Privacy Policy (the \"Policy\") describes what information is collected, how it is used, with whom it is shared and what rights the User has with respect to the User's data.\n\n1.3. Mooze adopts the principle of data minimization as a central pillar of its operation. The App was designed to function without the collection of personally identifiable data by Mooze.\n\n1.4. This Policy must be read together with the Terms of Use of the App.",
  "privacy_section_2_body": "2.1. All terms defined in the Terms of Use and used in this Policy have the same meanings assigned in Section 3 of the Terms of Use, unless expressly provided otherwise in this document.\n\n2.2. For purposes of this Policy, the following definitions also apply:\n(a) \"Personal Data\": any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person, within the meaning of the General Data Protection Law (Law No. 13,709/2018 — LGPD) or equivalent legislation.\n(b) \"Processing\": any operation performed with Personal Data, including collection, storage, use, sharing and deletion.\n(c) \"LGPD\": the Brazilian General Data Protection Law (Law No. 13,709/2018).\n(d) \"Controller\" and \"Processor\": the roles defined in the LGPD, applicable, where appropriate, to the relationships among Mooze, the User and the Regulated Partners.",
  "privacy_section_3_body": "3.1. DATA THAT MOOZE DOES NOT COLLECT OR STORE\nMooze DOES NOT collect in its systems or servers, with respect to Users of the App:\n(a) CPF, RG, passport or any civil identification document;\n(b) full legal name;\n(c) telephone number;\n(d) residential or mailing address;\n(e) date of birth;\n(f) biometric data (the device identification used is a one-way cryptographic hash and does not constitute personal biometrics);\n(g) the User's private keys, seed phrases or passwords;\n(h) images, photographs or videos: the device camera is accessed exclusively for reading QR codes (addresses and payment invoices), with processing performed locally on the device itself; no image or capture is collected, stored or transmitted to Mooze or to third parties.\n\n3.2. DATA THAT MOOZE COLLECTS\nMooze collects exclusively the following data:\n(a) APP ID: a technical device identifier, generated from operating system features (MediaDRM on Android devices, DeviceCheck on iOS devices). The APP ID is a one-way cryptographic hash that, on its own, does not allow personal identification of the User. It is used exclusively for fraud prevention and control of operational limits.\n(b) Wallet data: descriptors, addresses and public keys mathematically derived from the User's keys, used as a technical parameter for automated routing for the delivery of digital assets to the User during the performance of the Services; none of this data allows Mooze to move or access users' funds.\n(c) Blinding keys: cryptographic keys associated with Confidential Transactions on the Liquid Network, retained by Mooze exclusively for verification and reconciliation of transactions processed through the App in the functions involving Partner Infratechs via PIX.\n(d) Transaction data: records of the operations carried out through the App, including amounts, asset types, timestamps, transaction hashes and execution status. This data is retained for purposes of providing the Service, User support, reconciliation with partners and compliance with any legal obligations applicable to Mooze as a non-VASP entity.\n(e) Technical device data: generic information about the functioning of the App, such as operating system version, device model, installed App version and internal logs essential for support resolution and technical debugging. This data does not allow personal identification of the User.\n(f) Notification (push) token: a technical identifier generated by the Firebase Cloud Messaging service (Google LLC), used exclusively for sending operational notifications, such as transaction alerts, to the User's device. The token does not contain personally identifiable data, is not used for advertising, and its generation depends on notification permission granted by the User on the device.\n\n3.3. DEVICE PERMISSIONS\nThe App requests the following device permissions, always subject to the User's authorization in the operating system and for the purposes indicated below:\n(a) Camera: exclusively for reading QR codes (addresses and payment invoices), with local processing; images are not collected, stored or transmitted;\n(b) Notifications: exclusively for sending operational transaction alerts, through the Firebase Cloud Messaging service (Google LLC);\n(c) Biometric authentication or device credential: exclusively for locking local access to the App, processed by the device's own operating system; Mooze does not collect, access or store biometric data;\n(d) Network and internet access: for communication with the Bitcoin, Liquid Network and Lightning Network networks and with the infrastructure providers described in this Policy.",
  "privacy_section_4_body": "4.1. When the User carries out operations involving payment via PIX (Service A under the terms of use), the data necessary for processing the payment — including the payer's legal name, the payer's CPF, PIX key, bank details and other data necessary for compliance with KYC, AML and Travel Rule obligations — is collected and processed exclusively by the Regulated Partners in Brazil via indirect or direct services with our technology partners, within the limits of their respective activities via automations in systems linked to the Brazilian financial system.\n\n4.2. The Regulated Partners are:\n\n(a) PLEBIT.COM.BR Soluções em Tecnologia Ltda — CNPJ 43.375.652/0001-13;\n(b) Fits Instituição de Pagamento — CNPJ 13.203.354/0001-85;\n(c) Celcoin — CNPJ 13.935.893/0001-09;\n(d) PLEBZ INTERMEDIACAO DE PAGAMENTOS LTDA — CNPJ 45.808.899/0001-01.\n\nThis list of partners may be reduced or expanded, according to contractual modifications or changes and their availability.\n\n4.3. The collection, storage and processing of personal data by the Regulated Partners are governed by the respective privacy policies of those entities, in compliance with the LGPD and with the regulations of the Central Bank of Brazil. Each Regulated Partner acts as an autonomous Controller of the personal data it processes.\n\n4.4. Communication between Mooze's software and the Regulated Partners is limited to data strictly necessary for the automated routing of the operation (amount, public keys, destination wallet address, operation identifier, irreversible cryptographic identifiers derived from the payer's data and, when necessary, APP ID for anti-fraud purposes).\n\n4.5. Eulen.app LLC, as a technology infrastructure provider and issuer of the DEPIX token, and other partner infratechs may collect and process operational data necessary for the issuance of the tokens and related activities, in accordance with their own privacy policies, without Mooze acting as Controller of such data.",
  "privacy_section_5_body": "5.1. Mooze shares data exclusively in the following cases:\n(a) With the Regulated Partners and with Eulen.app LLC: data strictly necessary for the automated routing of operations (wallet addresses, amounts, operation identifiers and APP ID when necessary for anti-fraud purposes).\n(b) Upon a court order: Mooze may provide the data in its possession (APP ID, wallet addresses, blinding keys and related data collected) upon a valid court order issued by a competent court, subject to the rules on international recognition of judicial decisions applicable to entities headquartered in the Republic of the Marshall Islands.\n(c) For compliance with a legal obligation: when required by applicable law in the jurisdiction of the Republic of the Marshall Islands.\n(d) In MED procedures conducted by the Regulated Partners: technical provision of the APP ID and related data necessary when evidentiary reports of service execution or requirements arising from the need for their defense are requested through legal, regulatory or compliance demands.\n\n5.2. Mooze DOES NOT sell, rent, trade, assign or share data with third parties for purposes of marketing, advertising, behavioral analytics or any purpose not described in this Policy.\n\n5.3. To enable the sending of push notifications, the device notification token is processed by the Firebase Cloud Messaging service, provided by Google LLC, exclusively for that purpose. No other personal data is shared with Google for sending notifications.",
  "privacy_section_6_body": "6.1. When the User contacts Mooze through the support channels (e-mail suporte@mooze.app or Telegram), the data voluntarily shared by the User during the communication (such as username on messaging platforms, message content and any screenshots) will be used exclusively for the purpose of handling the request.\n\n6.2. Mooze does not, as a rule, associate support communication data with APP IDs or wallet addresses, except when the User voluntarily provides such information for the purpose of resolving a specific problem.",
  "privacy_section_7_body": "7.1. Mooze adopts reasonable technical and organizational measures, consistent with the applicable state of the art, to protect the data under its responsibility against unauthorized access, destruction, loss, alteration, or improper communication or disclosure.\n\n7.2. The data collected by Mooze is stored on protected infrastructure, with access controls and encryption in transit and at rest.\n\n7.3. Mooze cannot guarantee absolute security in the transmission of data over the internet or in electronic storage systems. The User acknowledges that no method of transmission or electronic storage is entirely immune to failures.",
  "privacy_section_8_body": "8.1. The data collected by Mooze is retained for the following periods:\n(a) APP ID: 5 (five) years from the last operation. After this period, it will be deleted, unless there is a legal retention obligation.\n(b) Wallet addresses, descriptors, public keys and blinding keys: 5 (five) years from the last operation, for purposes of verification, reconciliation and compliance with any legal obligations.\n(c) Transaction data: 5 (five) years from the date of the transaction.\n(d) Technical device data: deleted after 5 (five) years of inactivity.\n\n8.2. The above periods may be extended when necessary for: (a) compliance with a legal obligation; (b) compliance with a court order; (c) defense in judicial, administrative or arbitral proceedings; (d) improvement of anti-fraud systems, whether Mooze's own or joint with the Regulated Partners and Partner Infratechs, in the minimum necessary volume and in pseudonymized form whenever possible.",
  "privacy_section_9_body": "9.1. In observance of the LGPD, and notwithstanding that Mooze is not established in Brazil, Mooze recognizes the following rights of the User, to the extent applicable to the processing actually carried out:\n(a) confirmation of the existence of processing of pseudo-anonymous data;\n(b) evaluation of a request for deletion of the APP ID associated with the User's device and with the user of the Mooze software service\n\n9.2. The exercise of the rights provided for in clause 9.1 may be requested by the User through the channels indicated in Section 12 of this Policy.\n\n9.3. Mooze will respond to requests within 15 (fifteen) business days, under the LGPD, with a justified extension permitted in cases of technical complexity or volume.\n\n9.4. Deletion of the APP ID, once the request is fulfilled, will result in the deactivation of the device's access to the Services involving a FIAT reference (Service A and Merchant Mode under the terms of use). If the App is reinstalled, the device's access to the Services via FIAT means will remain blocked until a new formal request, sent from the same e-mail address used in the deletion request, with express and full acceptance of these Terms and the Privacy Policy.\n\n9.5. Certain data may be retained, or its deletion denied, even after a deletion request, when necessary for: (a) compliance with a legal obligation; (b) the regular exercise of rights in judicial, administrative or arbitral proceedings; (c) fraud prevention (especially if the user, with the user's APP ID, has pending involvement in payment disputes that have occurred, for example, MED), under art. 7, IX, and art. 16 of the LGPD; in accordance with the periods indicated in Section 8.",
  "privacy_section_10_body": "10.1. The data collected by Mooze is stored and processed on technology infrastructure located outside Brazilian territory.\n\n10.2. The data jurisdiction applicable to the processing activity carried out by Mooze is the Republic of the Marshall Islands, where Mooze is organized and operates.\n\n10.3. The operational data transmitted to the Regulated Partners during the performance of Service A under the terms of use is processed and stored in Brazil, under Brazilian jurisdiction and in compliance with the LGPD, under the exclusive responsibility of the Regulated Partners in their capacity as autonomous Controllers.\n\n10.4. The transfer of data from Brazil to Mooze's infrastructure (if any), to the extent it constitutes an international transfer for purposes of the LGPD, is carried out on the basis of the applicable legal grounds (art. 33 of the LGPD), including, as the case may be, the need to perform a contract to which the User is a party and compliance with a legal obligation.",
  "privacy_section_11_body": "11.1. Mooze reserves the right to change this Policy at any time by publishing the updated version in the App and at https://mooze.app/, with an indication of the date of the new version.\n\n11.2. Material changes will be communicated to the User through the App or the Telegram support channel.\n\n11.3. Continued use of the App after the publication of changes constitutes tacit acceptance of the updated Policy.",
  "privacy_section_12_body": "12.1. For questions or requests related to this Privacy Policy, the User may contact Mooze through the following official channels:\n(a) E-mail: suporte@mooze.app\n(b) Telegram support channel: https://t.me/+zkNS6KIDsEcyZDkx (also accessible via https://moozeapp.keepo.bio)\n(c) Automated FAQ via Telegram\n\n12.2. Formal notices related to personal data must be addressed to Mooze Labs LLC, Trust Company Complex, Ajeltake Island, Ajeltake Road, Majuro, Marshall Islands MH96960, Republic of the Marshall Islands, with a copy to the e-mail suporte@mooze.app; such forwarding details may be obtained by contacting this same e-mail address.\n\n12.3. Mooze will use efforts to respond to communications within 15 (fifteen) business days.",
